content.text:
Now implement fixes.

1. Slide 3 left column: flex column space-between, add closing line.
2. Slide 6: uniform gaps, quote after body.
3. Slide 7: remove hairline grid, cards on surface, consistent interiors, restructure buildline.

Let me apply CSS edits.

CSS for s3-body: currently
```
.s3-body{height:580px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 640px;gap:80px;
  padding:0 84px;align-items:center}
```
Change to align-items:stretch and make first child a flex column with padding. Simpler: keep grid, `align-items:center` on right; for left child add a class `s3-left` with `display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between;height:100%;padding:64px 0`.

Let me restructure s3-body to have explicit children classes.

Add:
```
.s3-left{display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between;height:100%;padding:70px 0}
.s3-close{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:22px;line-height:1.4;color:var(--muted);font-weight:300;font-style:italic;max-width:30ch}
```
Hmm using muted for closing line is weak. Use color:var(--gold)? or ink. Let's use `--ink2` with a gold em dash? Keep simple: serif italic, ink2.

Actually better closing: "The stock exists. What is missing is a mechanism." in serif 24px, ink color. Good.

Now slide 6.

Current `.why{display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between;height:100%}`.
Change to `justify-content:center;gap:32px;height:auto`.

But the right pane uses `.pane{padding:88px 84px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between}` so the `.why` child with height:auto will still be centered? `.pane` justify-content:space-between with a single child — it goes to top. So set the right pane's justify-content:center. It's inline style `padding-left:0`. I'll add class or inline `justify-content:center`.

Left pane: currently space-between with two children (top div, quote). Keep space-between? The headline block and quote. With quote at bottom, and pane height 900-176=724, there's a gap. The render showed paragraph ending at ~420 and quote at 750-880. That's a big gap but it's "anchored" so intentional. Hmm, on slide 6 the left column gap looked accidental because the right column had weird spacing. If I center the right column and keep left top+bottom, it may look balanced. But safer: make left content sequential (headline, body, quote) with margin-top 36 and center the whole block. Then the slide has a strong top-left headline. With pane justify-content:center.

Let me do: left pane justify-content:center, quote margin-top:38px. Right pane justify-content:center.

That leaves symmetric whitespace top and bottom — deliberate.

Slide 7:
```
.stack-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;grid-template-rows:1fr 1fr;
  gap:2px;background:rgba(245,239,229,.07);flex:1;min-height:0;margin:40px 0 0}
.stack-cell{background:var(--bg);padding:44px 46px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;
  justify-content:space-between;gap:24px}
```
Change to:
```
.stack-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;grid-template-rows:1fr 1fr;
  gap:20px;flex:1;min-height:0;margin:36px 0 0}
.stack-cell{background:var(--surface);padding:38px 42px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between}
.stack-cell .cell-body h3{...}
.stack-cell h3{font-size:34px;...margin-bottom:12px}
.stack-cell p{font-size:15.5px;...;margin-top:12px}
```
With `justify-content:space-between` and two children (role, div with h3+p), the role sits top and h3+p at bottom. Consistent across cells. Good.

Currently HTML: `<div class="role">` then `<div><h3>..</h3><p>..</p></div>`. So space-between works with current HTML. Just remove `gap:24px` (space-between handles it) and p margin.

Then buildline:
```
.s7{padding:78px 84px 70px}
```
stack-grid flex:1, buildline fixed at bottom.

New buildline:
```
.buildline{padding:32px 0 0}
.buildline .lab{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--gold);font-weight:500;margin-bottom:9px}
.buildline p{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:25px;line-height:1.3;color:var(--ink);font-weight:300;max-width:64ch}
```
And shorten text to "the matching, routing and confirmation logic that connects all four." to fit 1-2 lines.

Also stack cells at 2x2 with 20px gap: total width 1600-168=1432, each 706 wide. Padding 42 → content 622. h3 at 34px "OpenBoxes / OpenLMIS" might be wide ~ 380px, fine.

Height: 900 - 78 - 70 = 752 for content. Headline 2 lines at 54px ≈ 110. margin 36. buildline ~ 110. So grid = 752 - 110 - 36 - 110 = 496 → each row 238 with 20 gap. Cell padding 38*2=76 → 162 content: role 16 + h3 37 + p 2 lines 46 = 99. Fits with space-between.

Let's apply edits.

